<div class="view" id="view-ledger">
  <div id="ledgerstrip">connecting…</div>
  <!-- TWO TIERS, not three peer boxes (owner: "i dont really know
       what most of these things mean and no one else will either"). Tier 1 =
       the shared signed record, shown twice (as a feed, and grouped by
       author). Tier 2 = this machine's fast unsigned log. Each first line
       says what the box is in plain words; helm's internal word appears once,
       in parentheses, as a mapping to CLI output — never as the explanation. -->
  <div id="ledgertiers">
    <!-- TIER 0: THE LAND PIPELINE — moved here whole from the home tab
         (owner: "the ledger represents it all in addition to
         showcasing all of the dregginess we already do"; the collapsed home
         copy was the duplication he objected to). The lrsec element only
         RELOCATED: pollLr is always-on and renders into it by
         id, lrWire rebinds the row handlers after every render, so the whole
         card — honesty marks, UNKNOWN strips, closed footer — works here
         unchanged. The home tab keeps the one-line pipeline glance, which
         links to this tier. -->
    <section class="ltier" id="tierpipeline">
      <div class="ltierhead"><b>work landing · the pipeline</b><span>every
        change on its way into the shared code — who wrote it, who reviewed
        it, and whether git agrees it landed. one row is what helm calls a
        “land request”; alarms mean the record and reality disagree.</span></div>
      <section id="lrsec"></section>
    </section>
    <section class="ltier" id="tiersigned">
      <div class="ltierhead"><b>shared record · signed</b><span>chat posts and
        captured lessons, cryptographically signed as they land — the permanent,
        checkable copy of what the fleet said and decided. one signed entry is
        what helm calls a “cave turn”.</span></div>
      <div class="ltiergrid">
        <div class="lcard" id="cavecard">
          <h3>signed entries <span class="lsub" id="cavesub">checking whether signing is on…</span></h3>
          <div class="llegend"><span><span class="lbadge head">chat</span> a chat message</span>
            <span><span class="lbadge head">attest</span> a captured lesson</span>
            <span><span class="lbadge final">final</span> confirmed permanent</span></div>
          <div class="llegend" id="cavepulse">signing pulse: …</div>
          <div class="lrows" id="ledgerturns"><div class="empty">loading…</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lcard" id="cellcard">
          <h3>who signed <span class="lsub">the same entries, grouped by author</span></h3>
          <div class="llegend"><span><span class="ldot active"></span> signed &lt;2m ago</span>
            <span><span class="ldot quiet"></span> &lt;30m</span>
            <span><span class="ldot stuck"></span> silent &gt;30m</span>
            <span><span class="ldot"></span> nothing recent</span></div>
          <div class="lrows" id="ledgercells"><div class="empty">loading…</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ltier" id="tierlocal">
      <div class="ltierhead"><b>this machine only · not signed</b><span>helm’s
        fast working notes on this computer — instant, but they prove nothing
        beyond this host. the signed record is the proof copy.</span></div>
      <div class="lcard" id="nativecard">
        <h3>local activity <span class="lsub" id="nativesub">what helm did here, newest first</span></h3>
        <div class="llegend"><span><span class="lbadge final">chained</span> tamper-evident local note — not a signed entry</span>
          <span><span class="lbadge">receipt</span> plain operation log, append-only</span>
          <span style="margin-left:auto" id="nativehead">…</span></div>
        <div class="llegend" id="nativechat">chat pulse: …</div>
        <div class="lrows" id="ledgernative"><div class="empty">loading…</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
